ther I nor II"}, {"y0": 0.28181818166884565, "y1": 0.298181818032482, "x0": 0.14285715705824717, "x1": 0.8759398476410009, "t": "Q.12 Let G be an undirected complete graph on n vertices, where n > 2. Then, the number of"}, {"y0": 0.29939393936268277, "y1": 0.31395348805856504, "x0": 0.19360902395771223, "x1": 0.5225563961550697, "t": "different Hamiltonian cycles in G is equal to"}, {"y0": 0.3324986853959393, "y1": 0.3477338730420537, "x0": 0.2084824105254089, "x1": 0.25956270169945744, "t": "(A) n!"}, {"y0": 0.33107339321469365, "y1": 0.3477056767433394, "x0": 0.3833722659467416, "x1": 0.48128938623153666, "t": "(B) (n - 1)!"}, {"y0": 0.3298238464816936, "y1": 0.34750173448495625, "x0": 0.5563209139046869, "x1": 0.6053332206203142, "t": "(C) 1"}, {"y0": 0.32969696917877, "y1": 0.3590116276038411, "x0": 0.7330827081905736, "x1": 0.8120300744087818, "t": "(D) =-)!"}, {"y0": 0.4055232558306424, "y1": 0.42151162770860173, "x0": 0.14097744465315473, "x1": 0.1804511277622588, "t": "Q.13"}, {"y0": 0.414244185954189, "y1": 0.4302325578321483, "x0": 0.1936090234658472, "x1": 0.2650375914777619, "t": "Compute"}, {"y0": 0.41424418639525085, "y1": 0.4273255809375981, "x0": 0.265037594772634, "x1": 0.3082706769848848, "t": "lim"}, {"y0": 0.40531468019889405, "y1": 0.4188132269148328, "x0": 0.3232196348990456, "x1": 0.3741487851366043, "t": "x*-81"}, {"y0": 0.4242424244778109, "y1": 0.4360465115675807, "x0": 0.27631579046663574, "x1": 0.38909774562358984, "t": "x\u21923 2x2-5x-3"}, {"y0": 0.45494186063744835, "y1": 0.46969696978865283, "x0": 0.20864661709741916, "x1": 0.25187969930966997, "t": "(A) 1"}, {"y0": 0.453213379989592, "y1": 0.46975173584582275, "x0": 0.5581767903285754, "x1": 0.635432230684791, "t": "(B) 53/12"}, {"y0": 0.48401162806901454, "y1": 0.49999999994697386, "x0": 0.5582706759625582, "x1": 0.742481199131427, "t": "(D) Limit does not exist"}, {"y0": 0.4851631441265085, "y1": 0.5003019719417088, "x0": 0.2085508930279105, "x1": 0.2839303095145968, "t": "(C) 108/7"}, {"y0": 0.5392441860692567, "y1": 0.555232557947216, "x0": 0.1409774578101268, "x1": 0.8740601483928805, "t": "Q.14 Which one of the following statements is NOT correct about the B+ tree data structure used"}, {"y0": 0.5551515154217593, "y1": 0.5715151517853957, "x0": 0.19360903377064848, "x1": 0.5733082624699529, "t": "for creating an index of a relational database table?"}, {"y0": 0.5799418604999739, "y1": 0.5959302323779332, "x0": 0.1917293228811832, "x1": 0.47180451570635706, "t": "(A) B+ Tree is a height-balanced tree"}, {"y0": 0.595757575633643, "y1": 0.6133720928455569, "x0": 0.19172933143168724, "x1": 0.5545112746303427, "t": "(B) Non-leaf nodes have pointers to data records"}, {"y0": 0.6119186052771581, "y1": 0.6309090907285964, "x0": 0.19172933324591204, "x1": 0.58082706717702, "t": "(C) Key values in each node are kept in sorted order"}, {"y0": 0.6308139538164351, "y1": 0.645454545177741, "x0": 0.19172932162154924, "x1": 0.5883458597380999, "t": "(D) Each leaf node has a pointer to the next leaf node"}, {"y0": 0.6947674420068419, "y1": 0.7093023252169952, "x0": 0.14097744465315473, "x1": 0.1804511277622588, "t": "Q.15"}, {"y0": 0.6933139534843847, "y1": 0.7109090908782206, "x0": 0.18233082237718173, "x1": 0.8740601377731947, "t": "For La, b let us consider the regular language =(x|2=a23k 0rx=b10+12k,"}, {"y0": 0.7121212123429216, "y1": 0.7284848487065579, "x0": 0.19360903757766698, "x1": 0.8740601466955157, "t": "k \u2265 0}. Which one of the following can be a pumping length (the constant guaranteed by"}, {"y0": 0.7281976743662529, "y1": 0.7442424240018916, "x0": 0.19360902692949644, "x1": 0.4078947309652404, "t": "the pumping lemma) for L?"}, {"y0": 0.7616279071490761, "y1": 0.7763636364822024, "x0": 0.20864661709741916, "x1": 0.25187969930966997, "t": "(A) 3"}, {"y0": 0.7616279073774815, "y1": 0.7763636361326234, "x0": 0.385338346785476, "x1": 0.4266917279513661, "t": "(B) 5"}, {"y0": 0.7616279072902721, "y1": 0.7763636366233982, "x0": 0.5582706765